# Lessons Learned Log

Maintain [`docs/lessons-learned.md`](../../docs/lessons-learned.md) as a running record of incidents and their durable fixes.

## When to add an entry

After resolving any of the following, append an entry at the **top** (newest first):

- A production/runtime incident (something broke or silently stopped working)
- A bug with a non-obvious root cause or a misleading symptom
- A fix that future work could easily undo or repeat

Skip trivial changes (typos, formatting, obvious one-liners).

## Entry format

Use the template at the top of the doc: **Symptom, Root cause, Fix, Prevention, Files/refs**. Include enough paths, symbols, and log signatures that the next person avoids re-investigating.

## Relationship to other docs

- `docs/development-journal.md` = what was built/changed (features, architecture).
- `docs/lessons-learned.md` = what went wrong and how to avoid it again.

Cross-reference when relevant, but do not duplicate full content.
